WEBVTT

00:00.090 --> 00:01.920
Instructor: Next up, totally optional,

00:01.920 --> 00:05.250
like most of this section, just has to do with committing.

00:05.250 --> 00:06.780
I'm gonna show you how to make a commit

00:06.780 --> 00:09.420
using a GUI like GitKraken,

00:09.420 --> 00:12.750
and even if you're not interested in using a GUI,

00:12.750 --> 00:14.910
I still think it's worth checking out,

00:14.910 --> 00:18.390
because these GUIs can help show you your commits.

00:18.390 --> 00:20.040
They help you visualize things,

00:20.040 --> 00:22.615
but also it's nice to know that there are different ways

00:22.615 --> 00:25.350
of interacting with Git, and at the end of the day,

00:25.350 --> 00:27.900
we're still just working with that .git folder.

00:27.900 --> 00:29.160
It's just a different interface,

00:29.160 --> 00:31.110
different way of interacting with it.

00:31.110 --> 00:32.460
So I'm using GitKraken.

00:32.460 --> 00:34.500
I had a whole video on this early on

00:34.500 --> 00:36.300
where I talked about how to install it.

00:36.300 --> 00:37.200
It's very simple.

00:37.200 --> 00:40.830
You download it for free, and that's kind of it.

00:40.830 --> 00:43.530
And I'm just gonna open up this repo

00:43.530 --> 00:45.720
that we've been working in, my first novel.

00:45.720 --> 00:48.270
So if you have any repo you've created by now,

00:48.270 --> 00:50.460
whether it's from an exercise or you're following along,

00:50.460 --> 00:51.720
you have your own novel,

00:51.720 --> 00:54.300
whatever it is, we can open it with GitKraken.

00:54.300 --> 00:55.593
So here's GitKraken.

00:56.700 --> 00:59.730
I'm going to go to open a new repository.

00:59.730 --> 01:01.800
So if you open it up for the first time,

01:01.800 --> 01:03.210
it will probably look like this.

01:03.210 --> 01:06.030
It will ask you to open a repository.

01:06.030 --> 01:08.550
And then here is that folder I navigated to.

01:08.550 --> 01:10.800
I'm sorry I can't zoom in easily,

01:10.800 --> 01:12.810
but I just found my repository.

01:12.810 --> 01:17.040
So that same folder, my first novel, and I'm gonna open it.

01:17.040 --> 01:18.000
And there we are.

01:18.000 --> 01:20.850
We see my commit history right here.

01:20.850 --> 01:23.460
So right now, we're just visualizing the commits.

01:23.460 --> 01:26.700
This is basically what we see with a Git log.

01:26.700 --> 01:29.790
Unfortunately, it's not letting me zoom in much more either,

01:29.790 --> 01:31.170
but I hope you can see that.

01:31.170 --> 01:32.520
So we have our first one,

01:32.520 --> 01:34.500
start work on outline and main characters,

01:34.500 --> 01:37.890
all the way up to remove extra blank lines in chapter two.

01:37.890 --> 01:40.800
But what I wanna show you is how we make a new commit.

01:40.800 --> 01:43.170
So right now, our working tree is clean.

01:43.170 --> 01:46.380
I haven't made any changes at this point.

01:46.380 --> 01:49.530
I haven't diverged from what Git has committed,

01:49.530 --> 01:50.730
as you can see.

01:50.730 --> 01:52.110
But let's make some changes.

01:52.110 --> 01:53.790
What should we do?

01:53.790 --> 01:56.730
I'm gonna add some more to the characters file.

01:56.730 --> 02:00.000
So I just added some information about Myrtle Wilson,

02:00.000 --> 02:02.370
and here's some more information about George Wilson,

02:02.370 --> 02:04.380
two characters in the Great Gatsby

02:04.380 --> 02:06.300
that come up in chapter two.

02:06.300 --> 02:08.040
All right, so I'm gonna save that,

02:08.040 --> 02:11.040
and how about I add something to our moodboard?

02:11.040 --> 02:12.690
So I have these images in here.

02:12.690 --> 02:14.190
Let's add another image.

02:14.190 --> 02:16.110
Okay, so I downloaded two more images,

02:16.110 --> 02:18.480
one of alcohol and one of a billboard,

02:18.480 --> 02:21.300
thematically related in some way to the Great Gatsby.

02:21.300 --> 02:23.460
They're part of my moodboard,

02:23.460 --> 02:25.860
and both also licensed for me to use.

02:25.860 --> 02:29.700
So I'm gonna add those both into this moodboard folder.

02:29.700 --> 02:31.710
Okay, so I've made a couple of changes,

02:31.710 --> 02:33.840
and obviously, well I shouldn't say obviously,

02:33.840 --> 02:35.820
but hopefully, you're aware

02:35.820 --> 02:39.690
that I could check to see my status by using git status,

02:39.690 --> 02:42.870
and I would see that we modified characters.txt

02:42.870 --> 02:45.720
and that there are two new files in moodboard

02:45.720 --> 02:47.430
which are not being tracked.

02:47.430 --> 02:50.040
But this video is about using the GUI.

02:50.040 --> 02:52.440
If we take a look at the GUI, I get this message

02:52.440 --> 02:55.590
that says three file changes in working directory.

02:55.590 --> 02:58.230
So I can click here to view those file changes,

02:58.230 --> 03:01.260
or I can just click here where it says work in progress,

03:01.260 --> 03:03.720
and I wish I could make this larger,

03:03.720 --> 03:07.200
but what we see is unstaged files,

03:07.200 --> 03:11.460
characters.txt, and then moodboard bar

03:11.460 --> 03:13.980
and moodboard billboard, the two images.

03:13.980 --> 03:15.990
And you'll see that there's a little icon

03:15.990 --> 03:16.980
here with a pencil.

03:16.980 --> 03:19.890
That means I modified or edited that file.

03:19.890 --> 03:24.090
And here, this little plus sign means it's a new file.

03:24.090 --> 03:26.040
So I wanna make a commit, first,

03:26.040 --> 03:28.500
how about just with the characters changes.

03:28.500 --> 03:32.820
So I wanna stage characters, so I'm gonna click stage.

03:32.820 --> 03:36.690
Okay, so at this point, I have staged that one file,

03:36.690 --> 03:39.690
and actually, if I type git status over here,

03:39.690 --> 03:40.523
what do we see?

03:40.523 --> 03:43.950
Changes to be committed, characters.txt.

03:43.950 --> 03:45.540
So it was the same exact thing

03:45.540 --> 03:48.030
as me typing git add characters.

03:48.030 --> 03:50.430
But instead, I clicked stage,

03:50.430 --> 03:52.230
and then I'm gonna make my commit.

03:52.230 --> 03:54.720
So this first commit is just characters,

03:54.720 --> 03:57.510
so I add my commit message right there

03:57.510 --> 03:59.760
or I can type it over here,

03:59.760 --> 04:02.310
and my message will be something like

04:02.310 --> 04:05.997
add Wilsons to characters list.

04:12.360 --> 04:13.230
Okay?

04:13.230 --> 04:14.610
Or, yeah, that's fine.

04:14.610 --> 04:16.950
Add the Wilsons, maybe the Wilsons,

04:16.950 --> 04:19.620
So I added two of them, all right?

04:19.620 --> 04:22.083
And then I'll commit changes to that one file.

04:23.130 --> 04:25.020
And we see a new commit here,

04:25.020 --> 04:27.180
add the Wilsons to character list.

04:27.180 --> 04:30.870
And if I type git status, we now made a commit.

04:30.870 --> 04:34.290
We don't have this characters.txt staged anymore.

04:34.290 --> 04:36.930
And if I type git log, there it is.

04:36.930 --> 04:39.390
Add the Wilsons to characters list.

04:39.390 --> 04:43.050
So let's do a second commit now with the moodboard changes,

04:43.050 --> 04:46.170
so I'm gonna stage that new bar image

04:46.170 --> 04:47.913
and the billboard image,

04:48.840 --> 04:50.970
and then I group them together by staging them,

04:50.970 --> 04:52.342
and I'll make my commit,

04:52.342 --> 04:57.342
I don't know, add more, or how about expand,

04:58.350 --> 05:03.350
add two images to moodboard or something like that.

05:03.510 --> 05:05.070
Nothing amazing.

05:05.070 --> 05:06.750
But here's where I write that commit message,

05:06.750 --> 05:08.010
and here's where I commit.

05:08.010 --> 05:10.073
Before I do that, what do you expect me to see

05:10.073 --> 05:12.330
when I type git status?

05:12.330 --> 05:16.830
This is what we saw before, two untracked files,

05:16.830 --> 05:19.830
but now, they're both going to be committed.

05:19.830 --> 05:23.700
They are both staged because I clicked the stage button.

05:23.700 --> 05:26.520
So same process, just a different interface.

05:26.520 --> 05:31.520
I made changes, then I click to stage and I click to commit,

05:31.590 --> 05:36.270
or I use git add to stage and git commit to commit.

05:36.270 --> 05:37.103
All righty?

05:37.103 --> 05:40.083
So I'm gonna click commit changes to two files,

05:41.250 --> 05:42.083
and there we are.

05:42.083 --> 05:44.190
We have a new commit show up,

05:44.190 --> 05:46.833
and if I do git log, let's do our one line.

05:47.910 --> 05:48.840
There it is.

05:48.840 --> 05:50.520
Add two images to moodboard,

05:50.520 --> 05:52.920
add the Wilsons to character list.

05:52.920 --> 05:56.490
So that's just a quick intro to using a tool like GitKraken.

05:56.490 --> 05:57.900
Of course, the interface changes

05:57.900 --> 05:59.490
if you're using a different app,

05:59.490 --> 06:03.960
like SourceTree or, what else is there?

06:03.960 --> 06:06.990
GitTower? There's a couple of them. I can't remember.

06:06.990 --> 06:08.310
They all are similar, though.

06:08.310 --> 06:11.460
You click to stage, and then you click to commit,

06:11.460 --> 06:12.870
you type a message in,

06:12.870 --> 06:16.181
and this is just a nice educational tool, honestly,

06:16.181 --> 06:19.800
especially when we get to branching and merging,

06:19.800 --> 06:22.020
the diagrams over here are really helpful,

06:22.020 --> 06:23.400
but at this point, it's just another way

06:23.400 --> 06:25.373
of doing what we already know how to do.
